course: dictionary
lesson: 15947
title: Unsolicited
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unsolicited means not asked for. Look at the parts: un- means not, and solicited means asked for. So unsolicited is something nobody requested. «Nobody asked for his unsolicited advice about my homework.» Advice that comes without a request is unsolicited advice.
explain: «The letter was unsolicited mail, so Mum put it straight in the recycling.» The clue is that nobody asked for the letter. To check your meaning, swap in «not asked for» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Online, unsolicited emails, calls and messages can be scams, so they are not always safe. If a message arrives that you did not ask for, stop and ask a trusted adult before you click or reply.
fact: Unsolicited means not asked for.
fact: «Unsolicited advice» is advice someone gives when you did not ask for it.
fact: «Unsolicited mail» is post or emails that arrive without anyone requesting them.
fact: Unsolicited emails, calls or messages can be scams, so check with a trusted adult first.
fact: The opposite idea is «solicited», which means asked for.
exercise: «The shop sent unsolicited mail, but we never asked for it.» What does unsolicited mean? | Full of ink | *Not asked for | Very old | Sent by a friend
exercise: Which one is an example of unsolicited advice? | *Your sister tells you how to tie your shoes, though you never asked | Your teacher marks your spelling test | Mum asks what you would like for tea | A friend says, «Shall I help?» and you say yes
exercise: Ali gets a text from a number he does not know, offering free prizes he never entered for. Why should he be careful? | He asked for the message himself | *It may be an unsolicited scam message | Free prizes are always real | It must be from a friend, because it came to his phone
test: Which sentence uses unsolicited correctly? | *Nobody asked me, but the unsolicited advice kept coming | I asked for the advice, so it was unsolicited | The unsolicited sun came out at lunchtime | Mum made an unsolicited cake that I had asked for
test: Which word is the opposite of unsolicited, meaning asked for? | Unseen | Unfair | *Solicited | Unwanted
exam: What is the safest thing to do with an unsolicited message asking for your password? | Reply quickly to be polite | Give the password so they can help you | Click every link to see where it goes | *Ask a trusted adult before you click or reply
